          "text": "According to MoSPI data released on August 31, India's real GDP grew 7.8 percent in Q1 FY27, with real GDP estimated at Rs 81.36 lakh crore.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/ministers-dont-manufacture-data-goyal-hits-out-at-critics-for-questioning-gdp-figures/articleshow/133714520.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "cluster_id": 7,
          "text": "India's nominal GDP reached Rs 88.27 lakh crore in Q1 FY27, up 10.3 percent from Rs 80 lakh crore in Q1 FY26.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/ministers-dont-manufacture-data-goyal-hits-out-at-critics-for-questioning-gdp-figures/articleshow/133714520.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "cluster_id": 7,
          "text": "Former Finance Secretary Subhash Garg claimed that Q1 FY27 GDP growth in current prices would have been about 2.6 percent if last year's Q1 GDP had not been revised down from roughly Rs 86 lakh crore to Rs 80 lakh crore.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/ministers-dont-manufacture-data-goyal-hits-out-at-critics-for-questioning-gdp-figures/articleshow/133714520.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "cluster_id": 7,
          "text": "MoSPI stated that Q1 FY26 GDP was initially estimated at Rs 86.05 lakh crore under the 2011-12 base year, but was revised to Rs 80.32 lakh crore after introducing the 2022-23 base year series in February 2026.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/few-jobless-people-call-themselves-economists-piyush-goyal-jibes-at-opposition-critics-over-wrong-gdp-number-remark-101788358719506.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "cluster_id": 7,
          "text": "Sanjeev Sanyal, a member of the Prime Minister's Economic Advisory Council, stated that updating the GDP base year to 2022-23 was delayed due to the Covid-19 pandemic.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Scroll.in",
          "url": "https://scroll.in/latest/1095427/pms-economic-adviser-denies-allegations-of-centre-manipulating-gdp-data?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=public",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "cluster_id": 7,
          "text": "Congress leader Jairam Ramesh criticized the GDP calculations as statistical gymnastics, citing a gap between implied GDP inflation of 2.3 percent and wholesale price index inflation exceeding 9 percent.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Scroll.in",
          "url": "https://scroll.in/latest/1095427/pms-economic-adviser-denies-allegations-of-centre-manipulating-gdp-data?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=public",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "cluster_id": 7,
          "text": "SBI Group Chief Economic Adviser Soumya Kanti Ghosh spoke to NDTV regarding doubts raised about India's GDP growth data.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "NDTV",
          "url": "https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/sure-sign-of-intellectual-dishonesty-sbi-research-on-doubts-being-raised-on-gdp-growth-data-soumya-kanti-ghosh-group-chief-economic-adviser-sbi-11993614#publisher=newsstand",
          "source_kind": "summary"
        }
      ]
